<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 June in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 21 June, from 217 BCE to 1964.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hannibal.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">217 BCE <span class="tih-ago">1,809 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hannibal ambushes a Roman army at Lake Trasimene</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In morning mist on the lake shore, Hannibal trapped the consul Flaminius's army, killing about 15,000 Romans. The disaster led Rome to appoint Fabius Maximus as dictator.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1749 CE <span class="tih-ago">277 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward Cornwallis founds Halifax, Nova Scotia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British settlers arrived to build a fortified town as a counterweight to French Louisbourg. Halifax became a key naval base for Britain and later for Canada.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nova-scotia">Nova Scotia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1788 CE <span class="tih-ago">238 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Hampshire's ratification puts the US Constitution into effect</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">New Hampshire became the ninth state to ratify, the number required for the Constitution to take effect. The new federal government began work in 1789.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1813 CE <span class="tih-ago">213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wellington routs Joseph Bonaparte at Vitoria</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Wellington's Anglo-Portuguese and Spanish army broke the French in northern Spain, capturing their baggage train. Joseph fled, and French rule in Spain collapsed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1964 CE <span class="tih-ago">62 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Three civil rights workers are murdered in Mississippi</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">James Chaney, Andrew Goodman and Michael Schwerner were killed by Klansmen, with the involvement of local law officers, during Freedom Summer. Their deaths spurred support for the Voting Rights Act of 1965.</p></div></li></ol>
